WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.300
Welcome. This lesson treats a model update
as a release

2
00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:08.600
of a complete serving system, not as a new

3
00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:12.900
label attached to model weights. We will
version the entire

4
00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:17.200
serving unit, qualify the exact candidate
before traffic, stage it

5
00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:21.500
with bounded exposure, treat rollback as a
tested release, and

6
00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:25.800
close the lifecycle with evidence. We will
then repair a

7
00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:30.100
small local decision program whose
deliberate defect allows an incompatible

8
00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:34.400
rollback state to promote. The examples
are synthetic fixtures. They

9
00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:38.700
do not represent live infrastructure,
provider execution, authenticated people,

10
00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:43.000
production approvals, or rendered media.

11
00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:47.385
Version the entire serving unit. Start
with the immutable model

12
00:00:47.385 --> 00:00:51.769
revision and digest, but do not stop
there. Record the

13
00:00:51.769 --> 00:00:56.154
tokenizer, runtime, accelerator libraries,
container image, adapters, prompt

14
00:00:56.154 --> 00:01:00.538
templates, stop conditions, safety policy,
gateway contract, infrastructure

15
00:01:00.538 --> 00:01:04.923
configuration, evaluation set, telemetry
schema, and state schema. Include data

16
00:01:04.923 --> 00:01:09.308
dependencies that can affect serving
behavior or recovery. Any one

17
00:01:09.308 --> 00:01:13.692
of these can change quality, latency,
memory use, security, observability,

18
00:01:13.692 --> 00:01:18.077
or compatibility. Give the assembled
candidate one release identity and

19
00:01:18.077 --> 00:01:22.462
compare it with the currently approved
baseline. For every difference,

20
00:01:22.462 --> 00:01:26.846
record whether it is intentional, tested,
and owned. Unexplained drift

21
00:01:26.846 --> 00:01:31.231
is not a harmless detail. It is missing
release evidence.

22
00:01:31.231 --> 00:01:35.615
Retain the manifests, artifacts, immutable
locations, policy references, and

23
00:01:35.615 --> 00:01:40.000
deployment procedures needed to
reconstruct both releases. A mutable image

24
00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:44.385
tag or a remembered command is not enough.
SLSA provenance

25
00:01:44.385 --> 00:01:48.769
can describe where, when, and how an
artifact was produced,

26
00:01:48.769 --> 00:01:53.154
but provenance does not prove quality,
safety, capacity, or rollback

27
00:01:53.154 --> 00:01:57.538
compatibility. Those claims need their own
evidence. Required arrays in

28
00:01:57.538 --> 00:02:01.923
the operating packet are deliberately
nonempty. Accelerator libraries, adapters,

29
00:02:01.923 --> 00:02:06.308
prompt templates, stop conditions, and
drain conditions must not silently

30
00:02:06.308 --> 00:02:10.692
disappear as unknown evidence. If a
component is genuinely absent,

31
00:02:10.692 --> 00:02:15.077
represent that fact explicitly in the
production schema rather than

32
00:02:15.077 --> 00:02:19.462
disguising absence as an empty value.
Finally, do not infer

33
00:02:19.462 --> 00:02:23.846
capabilities from a model-family or
software-project name. Meta Llama, Qwen,

34
00:02:23.846 --> 00:02:28.231
DeepSeek, Mistral, Microsoft Phi, and
NVIDIA software occupy different project

35
00:02:28.231 --> 00:02:32.615
surfaces. Inventory the exact artifacts
and runtime actually deployed, including

36
00:02:32.615 --> 00:02:37.000
their contracts and recovery behavior.

37
00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:41.476
Here is a worked synthetic demonstration.
The proposed change is

38
00:02:41.476 --> 00:02:45.952
initially described as model version two.
The complete difference report

39
00:02:45.952 --> 00:02:50.429
reveals four additional changes: a new
tokenizer, an inference-server image

40
00:02:50.429 --> 00:02:54.905
update, a revised safety template, and a
telemetry field rename.

41
00:02:54.905 --> 00:02:59.381
A simple response check passes, but the
old client streaming

42
00:02:59.381 --> 00:03:03.857
parser breaks. Accelerator memory also
increases, and the dashboard appears

43
00:03:03.857 --> 00:03:08.333
incomplete because it expects the old
telemetry field. The arithmetic

44
00:03:08.333 --> 00:03:12.810
is simple but important. Suppose the
baseline uses 8 gigabytes

45
00:03:12.810 --> 00:03:17.286
for the serving process and the candidate
uses 9.2 gigabytes.

46
00:03:17.286 --> 00:03:21.762
The increase is 9.2 minus 8, which is 1.2

47
00:03:21.762 --> 00:03:26.238
gigabytes. Dividing 1.2 by 8 gives 0.15,
or a 15

48
00:03:26.238 --> 00:03:30.714
percent increase. That is a capacity
input, not a promotion

49
00:03:30.714 --> 00:03:35.190
decision. We now split the work into
gates. First, restore

50
00:03:35.190 --> 00:03:39.667
the application-owned telemetry contract
through a tested adapter. Second, test

51
00:03:39.667 --> 00:03:44.143
the old client parser against the new
server. Third, measure

52
00:03:44.143 --> 00:03:48.619
the tokenizer and memory changes in
representative quality and capacity

53
00:03:48.619 --> 00:03:53.095
cases. Fourth, record the revised safety
template as an intentional

54
00:03:53.095 --> 00:03:57.571
policy difference. The release identity is
therefore not merely model

55
00:03:57.571 --> 00:04:02.048
version two. It is the exact assembly and
its evidence.

56
00:04:02.048 --> 00:04:06.524
The lesson is causal: omitting surrounding
dependencies hides the very

57
00:04:06.524 --> 00:04:11.000
changes that can make rollback incomplete.

58
00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:15.214
Qualification asks whether this exact
assembly can replace the baseline

59
00:04:15.214 --> 00:04:19.429
in this exact environment. Verify
provenance, license disposition,

60
00:04:19.429 --> 00:04:23.643
signatures or documented alternatives,
dependency inventory, vulnerability

61
00:04:23.643 --> 00:04:27.857
findings, configuration policy,
environment compatibility, secret-handling

62
00:04:27.857 --> 00:04:32.071
evidence, and required resource
availability. Then test representative

63
00:04:32.071 --> 00:04:36.286
quality, safety, API compatibility, load,
cost, failure, and recovery cases.

64
00:04:36.286 --> 00:04:40.500
Use seven explicit gates. Quality covers
representative tasks and operational

65
00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:44.714
slices. Safety covers approved cases and
hard prohibitions. Security covers

66
00:04:44.714 --> 00:04:48.929
provenance, dependencies, vulnerabilities,
secret handling, and deployed

67
00:04:48.929 --> 00:04:53.143
configuration. Compatibility covers the
API, tokenizer, prompt, telemetry,

68
00:04:53.143 --> 00:04:57.357
runtime, and state contracts. Capacity
covers bounded load, latency, queues,

69
00:04:57.357 --> 00:05:01.571
memory, and failure behavior. Cost
compares measured resource use with

70
00:05:01.571 --> 00:05:05.786
a declared ceiling. Recovery proves that
the retained known-good unit

71
00:05:05.786 --> 00:05:10.000
and compatible state can be restored and
read back. Compare

72
00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:14.214
candidate and baseline by case and slice
rather than relying

73
00:05:14.214 --> 00:05:18.429
on one average. Define hard failures,
allowed deltas, uncertainty, owners,

74
00:05:18.429 --> 00:05:22.643
and waiver authority before seeing
results. Unknown, missing, placeholder, or

75
00:05:22.643 --> 00:05:26.857
contradictory evidence does not count as a
pass. A newer

76
00:05:26.857 --> 00:05:31.071
model-family name cannot override a failed
gate. The risk-management framework

77
00:05:31.071 --> 00:05:35.286
from NIST helps organize governance and
measurement, but a deployment

78
00:05:35.286 --> 00:05:39.500
still needs concrete thresholds and
accountable decision authority. A process

79
00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:43.714
that starts is not a capacity result.
Docker documents that

80
00:05:43.714 --> 00:05:47.929
containers have no resource constraints by
default, so CPU, memory,

81
00:05:47.929 --> 00:05:52.143
accelerator allocation, and host capacity
belong in tested configuration. Similarly,

82
00:05:52.143 --> 00:05:56.357
a security checklist is guidance, not
proof that a cluster

83
00:05:56.357 --> 00:06:00.571
enforces a setting. For latency
distributions, aggregate histogram buckets

84
00:06:00.571 --> 00:06:04.786
rather than averaging precomputed
quantiles. The lab values are

85
00:06:04.786 --> 00:06:09.000
deterministic fixture values, not
benchmark claims.

86
00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:13.267
Let us make a gate decision from supplied
fixture values.

87
00:06:13.267 --> 00:06:17.533
The safety guardrail observes a
refusal-rate delta of 0.05 and

88
00:06:17.533 --> 00:06:21.800
allows a maximum of 0.02. Subtracting the
maximum from the

89
00:06:21.800 --> 00:06:26.067
observed value gives 0.05 minus 0.02,
which equals 0.03 above

90
00:06:26.067 --> 00:06:30.333
the limit. Equivalently, 0.05 is 2.5 times
0.02. The result

91
00:06:30.333 --> 00:06:34.600
is safety FAIL, not pass. Now consider a
cost ceiling

92
00:06:34.600 --> 00:06:38.867
of 100 units per observation window. A
candidate total of

93
00:06:38.867 --> 00:06:43.133
96 is below the ceiling by 4 units, so

94
00:06:43.133 --> 00:06:47.400
cost passes this fixture. That one pass
cannot cancel the

95
00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:51.667
safety failure. Seven pass labels are also
not sufficient when

96
00:06:51.667 --> 00:06:55.933
compatibility evidence contradicts
rollback evidence. The decision function

97
00:06:55.933 --> 00:07:00.200
must inspect the evidence and the gate
statuses together. A

98
00:07:00.200 --> 00:07:04.467
missing state conversion, a false
compatibility claim, or a

99
00:07:04.467 --> 00:07:08.733
complete-manifest mismatch remains a
recovery failure even if the other

100
00:07:08.733 --> 00:07:13.000
six rows pass.

101
00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:17.360
A rollout converts qualification evidence
into bounded exposure. Choose the

102
00:07:17.360 --> 00:07:21.720
strategy for the actual environment and
consequence. Options include offline

103
00:07:21.720 --> 00:07:26.080
replacement, explicit route switching,
rolling replacement, canary traffic,

104
00:07:26.080 --> 00:07:30.440
blue-green service, and shadow comparison
that cannot create user-visible effects.

105
00:07:30.440 --> 00:07:34.800
Retain exact request-routing identity in
telemetry. The supplied worked packet

106
00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:39.160
declares a one percent simulated canary, a
ten-minute observation window,

107
00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:43.520
a 120-second drain timeout, a cost
ceiling, stop conditions, drain

108
00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:47.880
conditions, a decision owner, and an
executor. The names are

109
00:07:47.880 --> 00:07:52.240
synthetic exercise data, not authenticated
people or production approvals. Stop

110
00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:56.600
on any hard gate failure, unknown serving
identity, incompatible state,

111
00:07:56.600 --> 00:08:00.960
guardrail breach, or cost-ceiling breach.
Draining means stopping new candidate

112
00:08:00.960 --> 00:08:05.320
routing, allowing bounded in-flight
completion, handling remaining work under

113
00:08:05.320 --> 00:08:09.680
a declared policy, and restoring routes
only after baseline readiness

114
00:08:09.680 --> 00:08:14.040
and identity verification. Kubernetes
Deployment mechanics can change a workload

115
00:08:14.040 --> 00:08:18.400
template, but the application still owns
exact model identity, mixed-version

116
00:08:18.400 --> 00:08:22.760
behavior, state compatibility, and
postconditions. A shadow comparison is not

117
00:08:22.760 --> 00:08:27.120
automatically harmless. Its data use, side
effects, and policy must

118
00:08:27.120 --> 00:08:31.480
be approved. This local lab reads JSON
fixtures only. It

119
00:08:31.480 --> 00:08:35.840
invokes no model server, container
runtime, cluster API, cloud API,

120
00:08:35.840 --> 00:08:40.200
artifact store, approval service,
database, or telemetry backend. Passing

121
00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:44.560
the lab proves only that local decision
code handles supplied

122
00:08:44.560 --> 00:08:48.920
evidence consistently. A real integration
must resolve retained artifact identities,

123
00:08:48.920 --> 00:08:53.280
verify provenance and required signatures,
exercise the deployed runtime, read

124
00:08:53.280 --> 00:08:57.640
actual routing and telemetry, and obtain
authorization through the approved

125
00:08:57.640 --> 00:09:02.000
organizational system.

126
00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:06.250
Checkpoint. A newer candidate improves
average quality, but it fails

127
00:09:06.250 --> 00:09:10.500
one predeclared safety gate and breaks a
required client behavior

128
00:09:10.500 --> 00:09:14.750
during a canary. Exposure is only five
percent. What happens

129
00:09:14.750 --> 00:09:19.000
next, and what evidence must be retained?

130
00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:38.364
The correct action is to stop the rollout.
Five percent

131
00:10:38.364 --> 00:10:42.727
limits blast radius; it does not convert a
hard failure

132
00:10:42.727 --> 00:10:47.091
into an acceptable result. Preserve
candidate and baseline identities, exact

133
00:10:47.091 --> 00:10:51.455
routed requests or approved summaries, the
safety failure, the compatibility

134
00:10:51.455 --> 00:10:55.818
trace, the decision, and affected-state
evidence without retaining secrets or

135
00:10:55.818 --> 00:11:00.182
unnecessary request content. Remove
candidate traffic, verify the approved

136
00:11:00.182 --> 00:11:04.545
baseline, reconcile bounded in-flight
work, and issue a hold or

137
00:11:04.545 --> 00:11:08.909
reject disposition. A revised candidate
must return through qualification. If

138
00:11:08.909 --> 00:11:13.273
you continued because the candidate is
newer or its average

139
00:11:13.273 --> 00:11:17.636
improved, the causal error was allowing
aggregate improvement to override

140
00:11:17.636 --> 00:11:22.000
predeclared safety and compatibility
gates.

141
00:11:22.000 --> 00:11:26.289
Treat rollback as a controlled release
whose target is the

142
00:11:26.289 --> 00:11:30.579
retained known-good serving unit. Retain
the model and tokenizer artifacts,

143
00:11:30.579 --> 00:11:34.868
runtime and accelerator dependencies,
image, adapters, prompt templates, policy,

144
00:11:34.868 --> 00:11:39.158
gateway and infrastructure configuration,
evaluation identity, telemetry schema,

145
00:11:39.158 --> 00:11:43.447
state schema, secret references, and
recovery procedure. A Kubernetes

146
00:11:43.447 --> 00:11:47.737
Deployment revision rollback changes the
workload template managed by the

147
00:11:47.737 --> 00:11:52.026
Deployment controller. It does not
automatically restore an external

148
00:11:52.026 --> 00:11:56.316
database, undo a schema migration,
recreate a queue or vector

149
00:11:56.316 --> 00:12:00.605
index, recover an object store, restore
deleted artifacts, or make

150
00:12:00.605 --> 00:12:04.895
forward-written state readable by an older
runtime. State restoration and

151
00:12:04.895 --> 00:12:09.184
compatibility therefore need separate
evidence and procedures. The validator

152
00:12:09.184 --> 00:12:13.474
binds rollback evidence to the actual
baseline and candidate state

153
00:12:13.474 --> 00:12:17.763
schemas. Baseline state schema evidence
must equal the baseline manifest

154
00:12:17.763 --> 00:12:22.053
value, and candidate evidence must equal
the candidate manifest value.

155
00:12:22.053 --> 00:12:26.342
A compatible-rollback claim must agree
with a passing recovery gate

156
00:12:26.342 --> 00:12:30.632
and non-placeholder compatibility
evidence. A false claim must agree with

157
00:12:30.632 --> 00:12:34.921
a failed recovery gate. Consider the
supplied worked example. Baseline

158
00:12:34.921 --> 00:12:39.211
release svc-2026-09-01 uses
conversation-v1. Candidate release

159
00:12:39.211 --> 00:12:43.500
svc-2026-09-20 uses conversation-v2. There
is no tested reverse conversion, so

160
00:12:43.500 --> 00:12:47.789
rollback compatibility is false and
recovery fails. Six other gates

161
00:12:47.789 --> 00:12:52.079
pass. The deliberate defect discards
recovery while collecting failures, so

162
00:12:52.079 --> 00:12:56.368
the starter promotes. The repaired
predicate collects every gate whose

163
00:12:56.368 --> 00:13:00.658
status is not pass. The repaired result
rejects and reports

164
00:13:00.658 --> 00:13:04.947
recovery. During the simulated rehearsal,
the safety value is 0.05

165
00:13:04.947 --> 00:13:09.237
and the maximum is 0.02, so 0.05 is
greater than

166
00:13:09.237 --> 00:13:13.526
0.02. The guardrail is FAIL and the action
is STOP_AND_DRAIN.

167
00:13:13.526 --> 00:13:17.816
The exposure is one percent, the
observation window is ten

168
00:13:17.816 --> 00:13:22.105
minutes, and the drain timeout is 120
seconds. The rollback

169
00:13:22.105 --> 00:13:26.395
target and readback release are both
svc-2026-09-01. Readiness is true.

170
00:13:26.395 --> 00:13:30.684
The complete readback manifest equals the
immutable baseline, so

171
00:13:30.684 --> 00:13:34.974
READBACK_COMPLETE_MANIFEST_MATCH is true
and ROLLBACK_VERIFIED is true. That

172
00:13:34.974 --> 00:13:39.263
comparison covers release ID, model,
tokenizer, runtime, accelerator libraries,

173
00:13:39.263 --> 00:13:43.553
image, adapters, prompt templates, safety
policy, gateway contract, infrastructure

174
00:13:43.553 --> 00:13:47.842
configuration, evaluation set, telemetry
schema, and state schema. One matching

175
00:13:47.842 --> 00:13:52.132
model digest is not enough. This is
simulated fixture processing,

176
00:13:52.132 --> 00:13:56.421
not proof that live traffic was exposed, a
drain occurred,

177
00:13:56.421 --> 00:14:00.711
external state was restored, artifacts
were recovered, or an approval

178
00:14:00.711 --> 00:14:05.000
was issued.

179
00:14:05.000 --> 00:14:09.286
Let us distinguish identity from
postcondition. Matching the baseline model

180
00:14:09.286 --> 00:14:13.571
digest proves only that one artifact was
selected. It does

181
00:14:13.571 --> 00:14:17.857
not prove that the tokenizer, runtime,
image, adapters, policy, gateway,

182
00:14:17.857 --> 00:14:22.143
infrastructure, evaluation identity,
telemetry schema, or state schema match.

183
00:14:22.143 --> 00:14:26.429
It also does not prove readiness. The
correct logical result

184
00:14:26.429 --> 00:14:30.714
requires every required comparison to be
true. If there are

185
00:14:30.714 --> 00:14:35.000
fourteen independent identity and
readiness checks and thirteen are true,

186
00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:39.286
the complete match is false, not thirteen
fourteenths acceptable. Rollback

187
00:14:39.286 --> 00:14:43.571
is a conjunction, not an average. The same
reasoning applies

188
00:14:43.571 --> 00:14:47.857
to state. If the candidate wrote
conversation-v2 and the baseline

189
00:14:47.857 --> 00:14:52.143
reads conversation-v1, a route switch
alone leaves a postcondition boundary

190
00:14:52.143 --> 00:14:56.429
unresolved. Provide a tested conversion, a
compatible reader, restoration, or

191
00:14:56.429 --> 00:15:00.714
a documented compensating path. Otherwise
recovery fails and promotion must

192
00:15:00.714 --> 00:15:05.000
be blocked.

193
00:15:05.000 --> 00:15:09.211
Close the lifecycle with an evidence
ledger. Record who proposed,

194
00:15:09.211 --> 00:15:13.421
reviewed, approved, executed, paused,
rolled back, and verified a change,

195
00:15:13.421 --> 00:15:17.632
while distinguishing synthetic exercise
records from authenticated organizational

196
00:15:17.632 --> 00:15:21.842
records. Retain timestamps, immutable
identities, test outputs, exposure,

197
00:15:21.842 --> 00:15:26.053
decisions, residual risks, exceptions,
expiry, and follow-up without retaining

198
00:15:26.053 --> 00:15:30.263
secrets or unnecessary request content.
Evidence must make successful and

199
00:15:30.263 --> 00:15:34.474
failed decisions reconstructable. Keep
rejected candidate combinations with an

200
00:15:34.474 --> 00:15:38.684
explicit disposition and failed gates. Use
those failures to update

201
00:15:38.684 --> 00:15:42.895
evaluation cases, thresholds, capacity
assumptions, compatibility manifests,

202
00:15:42.895 --> 00:15:47.105
state-migration tests, and runbooks. A
test log is evidence about

203
00:15:47.105 --> 00:15:51.316
software behavior, not authorization to
expose users. Evidence also expires.

204
00:15:51.316 --> 00:15:55.526
When infrastructure, traffic, policy,
data, graders, or dependencies change,

205
00:15:55.526 --> 00:15:59.737
rerun affected gates instead of treating
an old approval as

206
00:15:59.737 --> 00:16:03.947
permanent. A complete activity preserves
complete baseline and candidate manifests,

207
00:16:03.947 --> 00:16:08.158
all seven gates, bounded exposure,
observation, stop, drain, cost, owner,

208
00:16:08.158 --> 00:16:12.368
executor, rollback verification, and
residual risks. It rejects contradictory

209
00:16:12.368 --> 00:16:16.579
rollback evidence. A deny-all
implementation, a hardcoded release

210
00:16:16.579 --> 00:16:20.789
identifier, a weakened validator, altered
immutable tests, placeholder evidence, or

211
00:16:20.789 --> 00:16:25.000
partial readback does not satisfy the
activity.

212
00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:29.231
Now plan and rehearse a reversible update.
Create baseline and

213
00:16:29.231 --> 00:16:33.462
candidate manifests that identify the
model, tokenizer, runtime, image,

214
00:16:33.462 --> 00:16:37.692
adapters, policies, configuration,
infrastructure, evaluation set, telemetry

215
00:16:37.692 --> 00:16:41.923
schema, and state schema by immutable
identity. Define quality, safety,

216
00:16:41.923 --> 00:16:46.154
security, compatibility, capacity, cost,
and recovery comparisons with hard gates

217
00:16:46.154 --> 00:16:50.385
and authorized reviewers. Select a
workstation, container, on-premises, edge,

218
00:16:50.385 --> 00:16:54.615
